         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question-button" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-2">
               How much sleep does a cat need?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="faq-answer-2">
             <p>Most adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Kittens and senior cats often sleep even longer because growth and aging both demand more rest.</p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question-button" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-3">
               Why does my cat knead blankets or laps?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="faq-answer-3">
             <p>Kneading is a leftover comfort behavior from kittenhood. Many cats do it when they feel content, are settling down, or are marking a favorite spot with scent glands in their paws.</p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question-button" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-4">
               How can I help my cat drink more water?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="faq-answer-4">
             <p>Try a pet fountain, place several bowls around the home, and offer wet food if your veterinarian agrees. Many cats prefer fresh, moving water away from their food dish.</p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question-button" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-5">
               Why does my cat stare out the window for so long?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="faq-answer-5">
             <p>Windows provide enrichment. Cats enjoy watching birds, insects, people, and changes in light because it stimulates their hunting instincts without requiring them to leave a safe space.</p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </div>
     </main>

     <footer>
       Built with semantic HTML, keyboard-friendly disclosure buttons, and a dark, high-contrast finish.
     </footer>
   </div>

   <script>
