  <a class="skip-link" href="#maincontent">Skip to main content</a>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Cat care FAQ</p>
      <h1>Common questions about cats</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Quick answers about feline behavior, routines, and health habits. Open any question to reveal the answer.
      </p>
    </header>

    <main id="maincontent" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="example">
          <h2>
            <button class="question-button" id="faq-question-1" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-1">
              Why do cats purr?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div class="details" id="faq-answer-1" aria-labelledby="faq-question-1">
            <p>Cats often purr when they feel relaxed and safe, but they may also purr to self-soothe when stressed or recovering from discomfort.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2>
            <button class="question-button" id="faq-question-2" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-2">
              How much sleep does a cat need?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div class="details" id="faq-answer-2" aria-labelledby="faq-question-2">
            <p>Most adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day. Kittens and senior cats often sleep even longer because growth and aging both demand more rest.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2>
            <button class="question-button" id="faq-question-3" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-3">
              Why does my cat knead blankets or laps?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div class="details" id="faq-answer-3" aria-labelledby="faq-question-3">
            <p>Kneading is a leftover comfort behavior from kittenhood. Many cats do it when they feel content, are settling down, or are marking a favorite spot with scent glands in their paws.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2>
            <button class="question-button" id="faq-question-4" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-4">
              How can I help my cat drink more water?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div class="details" id="faq-answer-4" aria-labelledby="faq-question-4">
            <p>Try a pet fountain, place several bowls around the home, and offer wet food if your veterinarian agrees. Many cats prefer fresh, moving water away from their food dish.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2>
            <button class="question-button" id="faq-question-5" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-answer-5">
              Why does my cat stare out the window for so long?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div class="details" id="faq-answer-5" aria-labelledby="faq-question-5">
            <p>Windows provide enrichment. Cats enjoy watching birds, insects, people, and changes in light because it stimulates their hunting instincts without requiring them to leave a safe space.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer>
      Built with semantic HTML, keyboard-friendly disclosure buttons, and a dark, high-contrast finish.
    </footer>
  </div>

  <script>
    const disclosureButtons = document.querySelectorAll(".question-button");

    disclosureButtons.forEach((button) => {
      const panelId = button.getAttribute("aria-controls");
      const panel = panelId ? document.getElementById(panelId) : null;

      if (!panel) {
        return;
      }

      const togglePanel = (expand) => {
        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(expand));
        panel.hidden = !expand;
      };

      button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
      panel.hidden = true;

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
        togglePanel(!isExpanded);
      });

      button.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
        if (event.key === "Escape" && button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true") {
          event.preventDefault();
          togglePanel(false);
          button.focus();
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
